The AirPort Extreme is a [[residential gateway]] combining the functions of a [[router (computing)|router]], [[network switch]],  [[wireless access point]] and [[network-attached storage|NAS]] as well as varied other functions, and one of Apple's former [[AirPort]] products. The latest model, the 6th generation, supports [[IEEE 802.11ac|802.11ac]] networking in addition to older standards. Versions of the same system with a built-in network-accessible [[hard drive]] are known as the [[AirPort Time Capsule]].

Apple discontinued developing its lineup of wireless routers in 2016, but {{As of|2023|lc=yes}} continues limited hardware and software support.<ref name=AppleVintageObsolete/>

